--!nonstrict
--[[
	Robscript team - NFT Battle
	Case opening and inventory automation for the NFT Battle case opener (place "Ugc").

	UI framework: Robly Airflow (https://github.com/bobloscript/Robly_Airflow)

	Game surface this script drives (verified against the live client):
	  * ReplicatedStorage.Events.OpenCase:InvokeServer(caseName, amount, {})
	      -> true   opened
	      -> false  refused
	      -> "Buy"  the case needs a Robux product, the client should open a purchase prompt
	  * ReplicatedStorage.Events.Inventory:FireServer("Sell", itemName)
	      only honoured for the inventory cards the game itself rendered, so selling goes
	      through each card's own Sell signal instead of a hand-made FireServer call.
	  * ReplicatedStorage.Info.Cases / .PaidCases / .Gifts
	  * PlayerGui.MainGui.Topbar.Right.Stars
	  * PlayerGui.MainGui.Pages.Profile.MainFrame.Scroll.Default

	Pacing: the server accepts roughly one open request every 5.7 seconds (measured: an
	attempt 5.7s after the previous success goes through, anything below 4s is refused, and
	amount 1 and amount 10 share the same window). Refused attempts are cheap but useless,
	so the loop waits out the cooldown instead of hammering the remote.

	Strict typing is off on purpose: the executor injects globals (getconnections, firesignal,
	loadstring, HttpGet) that a strict analyser cannot see.
]]

